---
title: Chicken Stroganoff
description: Seared chicken and baby bella mushrooms in a creamy mustard-Worcestershire sauce over buttered egg noodles.
source: https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a25647973/chicken-stroganoff-recipe/
author: Lena Abraham (Delish)
servings: 4
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 50 minutes
time required: 1 hour
course: main
cuisine: Russian-American
tags:
  - chicken
  - mushrooms
  - pasta
  - creamy
  - skillet
  - stroganoff
  - scaling
---

Cook @egg noodles{12%oz} in a #large pot{} of boiling salted water according to package directions until al dente; drain. Toss with @butter{2%tbsp} while still hot and set aside.

In a #large skillet{} over medium heat, heat @vegetable oil{1%tbsp}. Add @boneless skinless chicken breasts{1%lb}(cut into 1-inch pieces) and sear until golden on all sides, about ~{8-10%minutes}, working in batches if needed. Season with @kosher salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{}. Transfer the chicken to a #large bowl{}.

Add @extra-virgin olive oil{1%tbsp} to the skillet over medium heat. Add @brown mushrooms{1%lb}(baby bella, thinly sliced) and cook until golden and tender, about ~{8-10%minutes}. Transfer to the bowl with the chicken.

Add the remaining @extra-virgin olive oil{1%tbsp} and @onion{1/2}(large, chopped). Cook until softened, about ~{6%minutes}. Add @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and @fresh thyme{2%tsp}(leaves) and cook until fragrant, about ~{2%minutes} more.

Stir in @chicken broth{4%cups}(low-sodium), @Dijon mustard{2%tsp}, and @Worcestershire sauce{1%tsp} and bring to a simmer.

In a #small bowl{}, whisk some of the hot broth into @cornstarch{2%tbsp} until smooth. Stir the slurry into the skillet along with the reserved chicken and mushrooms. Continue to simmer until thickened by about half, about ~{10-12%minutes}.

Remove from heat and stir in @sour cream{2%tbsp}. Season with @kosher salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{} to taste.

Spoon the chicken mixture over the buttered egg noodles and garnish with a dollop of sour cream and @fresh parsley{2%tbsp}(chopped).
